<BaseLayout title="2021 S60 model range and specifications">
  <h1>2021 S60 model range and specifications</h1>
  <p>This page describes the North American 2021-model-year, third-generation Volvo S60 range. Equipment on an individual vehicle depends on market, build date, trim, packages, and VIN.</p>
  <h2>Powertrain range</h2>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Designation</th><th>Engine / propulsion</th><th>Published output</th><th>Drive layout</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th>T5</th><td>2.0 L turbocharged four-cylinder gasoline</td><td>250 hp / 258 lb-ft</td><td>FWD or AWD, depending on configuration</td></tr>
    <tr><th>T6</th><td>2.0 L turbocharged and supercharged four-cylinder gasoline</td><td>316 hp / 295 lb-ft</td><td>AWD</td></tr>
    <tr><th>T8 Recharge</th><td>2.0 L twin-charged gasoline engine plus plug-in-hybrid electric drive</td><td>400 hp combined system output (version dependent)</td><td>AWD; rear axle is electrically driven</td></tr>
    <tr><th>T8 Polestar Engineered</th><td>High-output T8 plug-in-hybrid powertrain</td><td>Up to 415 hp combined system output</td><td>AWD; performance-specific chassis and equipment</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <p class="note"><strong>Powertrain note.</strong> T5, T6, and T8 identify different propulsion systems, not just trim levels. T5 is turbocharged; T6 adds a supercharger; T8 adds an electric rear drive system and rechargeable high-voltage battery. T8 service work involves high-voltage safety requirements and is not covered by ordinary gasoline-engine procedures.</p>
  <h2>Trim and equipment differences</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Momentum:</strong> comfort-oriented entry trim; available equipment and standard features vary by powertrain.</li>
    <li><strong>R-Design:</strong> sportier exterior and interior appearance, with distinct seats and trim on applicable configurations.</li>
    <li><strong>Inscription:</strong> more luxury-oriented appearance and interior appointments.</li>
    <li><strong>Recharge-specific trims:</strong> T8 models used market-specific naming such as Inscription Expression; Polestar Engineered is a separate performance specification.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note"><strong>Trim is not a reliable parts identifier.</strong> Wheels, brakes, seats, lighting, audio, driver-assistance equipment, and suspension can depend on option packages and production specification—not just the trunk badge.</p>
  <h2>Transmission and chassis</h2>
  <p>An eight-speed automatic is used across the North American 2021 S60 range, but transmission variants, calibration, and fluid requirements can differ. T5 FWD, T5 AWD, T6 AWD, and T8 plug-in-hybrid drivetrains must not be treated as interchangeable.</p>
  <h2>Individual vehicle identification</h2>
  <p>The original reference car for some owner notes is a 2021 S60 T5 Inscription AWD in Denim Blue. That is one configuration within the broader model range—not the default specification for every page.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm engine code and production date.</li><li>Confirm FWD, mechanical AWD, or T8 plug-in-hybrid AWD.</li><li>Confirm transmission and rear-drive hardware before selecting fluids or parts.</li><li>Confirm brake package, wheel size, tire specification, and suspension options.</li><li>Confirm trim, packages, and market-specific equipment.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Use VIN-specific Volvo build information and the labels on the vehicle. Keep the full VIN private and out of this public website.</p>
